`, `_ends`, `_flags`                                                                                                  |","+| nodes written, column capacity, growth                | `_nodeCount`, `_nodeCapacity`, `_growNodeColumns`                                                                                       |","+| a node's list of children, as a span                  | `_listStarts`, `_listLengths` into `_listItems`, filled up to `_listItemTop`                                                            |","+| the empty column a released one shares                | `EMPTY_U8`, `EMPTY_U16`, `EMPTY_I32`, one per typed-array kind                                                                          |","+| the path object and its class                         | `A`, `<Language>SyntaxPath`                                                                                                             |","+| regrow hint and peak from a parse                     | `_nodeGrowHint`, `_listItemGrowHint`, `_nodePeak`, `_listItemPeak`                                                                      |","+| capacity above which columns are freed                | `_SHRINK_CAPACITY`                                                                                                                      |","+| reset before a parse, free after it                   | `_resetColumns`, `_releaseColumns`                                                                                                      |","+| write a node                                          | `_makeNode` (`_makeLeaf`/`_makeContainer` in CSS), `_makeAttr`                                                                          |","+| line and column converter                             | `_locConverter`, a `LocConverter` given its language's line terminators (JavaScript's `getLineInfo` keeps acorn's answer inside a CRLF) |","+| the caller's `parseError` and the reporter calling it | `_parseError`, `_reportParseError`                                                                                                      |","+| walk position                                         | `_walkNode`, `_walkIndex`, `_walkParent`                                                                                                |","+| walk control and visitors                             | `_walkSkipped`, `_walkStopped`, `_walkVisitors`, `_walkHalted`                                                                          |","+| character-class table                                 | `_CHAR_CLASS`                                                                                                                           |","+| the parse input, cleared on release                   | `_S._input` (CSS keeps the caller's string before NUL replacement as `_originalInput`)                                                  |"," "," The `_` marks a module-private name in CSS and HTML; JavaScript's module-level names carry none (`walkNode`, `nodeGrowHint`, `SHRINK_CAPACITY`, `CHAR_CLASS`), and the rest of the name is the same."," "],"additions":17,"deletions":17,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/css/CssParser.js","lines":["@@ -1344,7 +1344,7 @@ class CssParser extends Parser {"," \t\t\tmodule.buildMeta.needIdInConcatenation = true;"," \t\t}"," ","-\t\tconst locConverter = new LocConverter(source, true);","+\t\tconst locConverter = new LocConverter(source, \"css\");"," "," \t\t/**"," \t\t * Source location of a byte range. `LocConverter#get` mutates and returns itself, so snapshot between the two calls."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"lib/css/syntax-parser.js","lines":["@@ -2355,7 +2355,7 @@ class TokenStream {"," \tconstructor("," \t\tinput,"," \t\tpos = 0,","-\t\tlocConverter = new LocConverter(input, true),","+\t\tlocConverter = new LocConverter(input, \"css\"),"," \t\tonComment = undefined"," \t) {"," \t\t/** @type {string} */","@@ -2574,7 +2574,7 @@ const normalizeIntoToke